[h1]Phobos Framework[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.41.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

The shared toolbox behind the Phobos mods. On its own it adds no new machinery; install it with the Phobos content mods that need it, and it keeps their controls, crew work and supplies behaving the same way from one machine to the next.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Shared control panels: Apply/Discard settings, store selection, crew standing orders and training, with native-looking buttons and one volume control for the quiet completion alerts.
[*]Crew standing orders: give crew a chosen job and approved supplies. Orders begin disabled; shifts, needs, access and the game's AutoTask and Haul duties still apply. Crew can take supplies from anywhere aboard, nearest first, as the game's own Reload job does.
[*]Crew study Phobos specialities at powered terminals through the game's own study actions, and AutoTask crew choose them on their own.
[*]Supported onboard work carries on through time-skip. Exterior work and flight pause and wait for Resume.
[*]Construction, supply transfers and station purchases check materials, space and power. A full destination keeps cargo where it was; nothing is silently thrown away.
[*]Shared bulk storage for silos and reservoirs, with the object's mass kept honest and station purchase through the refuelling kiosk's Bulk supplies view.
[*]When a Phobos autopilot switches ship sensors on, it remembers what it switched and turns off only those. Your own switch always wins, and you are told every time in the crew log and on the nav map.
[*]Shared merchant stock, salvage finds, repair, Restore and dismantling rules for the content mods, without refilling or rewriting existing shops or saves.
[*]Shared translation support that falls back to English when a line is missing.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*]Install Framework together with Phobos Shipbreaker, Auto Nav, Agriculture or Manufacturing. Each content mod names the Framework version it needs.
[*]Right-click Phobos equipment and choose Control Panel for its settings and crew orders.
[*]In the F3 console, phobosframework status reports what loaded; phobosframework crew shows who is studying or could take each order step, and why.
[/list]
Mod authors: see the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/development/framework-author-guide.md]Framework author guide[/url].

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[*]Optional, not required: Valtora's Ship's Water, LOGUSS's Common Sense modules and jossla's Study at Terminals work alongside it.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Framework and the Phobos content mods you want.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load. Do the same after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[*]Used the repository's local installer before? Remove those local copies first so only one copy loads. See the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/installing-mods.md]installation guide[/url].
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
Ordinary saves are supported. Keep Framework and the content mods installed while a save uses their content; removing them is not a clean uninstall. Updating does not refill existing shops or old loot containers. Saved contents or settings that cannot be checked safely stop the affected work for inspection rather than being guessed at. Automated checks pass, but in-game evaluation of recent features is ongoing.

